From 4eac1e6b6e6d5e8a41b098cf506e572666c1505a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fbalazsy <frantisekbalazsy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:29:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] drm/apple: desktop HDMI: report the unplug, move a
 two-pipe Type-C display onto the freed hybrid

On a desktop 26.x processor the HDMI HPD handler left disconnects to the
firmware.  The J616s's DP-to-HDMI converter (a Parade DP855) keeps its DP
link up without a sink, so the firmware never reports an unplug: the
HDMI connector stayed connected and the hybrid pipeline busy until the
next plug.  Debounce both edges for 500 ms; when HPD stays low, report
the unplug as a CRTC power-off with HPD low does, and start the HDMI
presence hold, which frees the hybrid when it expires.

A Type-C display wider than one pipe that came while HDMI held the
hybrid sits on the Type-C-only pipeline, which pairs with nothing above
it.  When the hybrid becomes free again, move such a display onto it,
as a replug does, so that it gets both pipes.

While the hybrid drives a Type-C display, an HDMI plug only waits: the
cold-plug HPD pulse would have hit the Type-C display's link.
